1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Shipyard Solver Lab is a preparation workbench for the Optimization Grand Challenge.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:26,000
The goal is a repeatable contest loop: load, solve, validate, score, inspect, and improve.

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:38,000
The first panel keeps the claim boundary visible. This is toy data plus a public OGC example, not leaderboard evidence.

4
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:51,000
The official example projection proves that the repository can ingest the public OGC baseline package.

5
00:00:51,000 --> 00:01:05,000
The official checker smoke test proves exact operations format and public feasibility checker integration.

6
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The portfolio candidate wraps the public greedy baseline, searches bay assignments, and keeps the best feasible solution.

7
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:39,000
On the public example, it improves the greedy reference and matches the static assignment lower bound after 1,024 assignments.

8
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:51,000
The package panel shows the next artifact: an official candidate zip with myalgorithm.py at the archive root.

9
00:01:51,000 --> 00:02:04,000
The yard layout and table are generated from JSON outputs, so the dashboard is tied to real solver artifacts.

10
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:20,000
When the official platform opens, this project can continue from evidence instead of starting from scratch.
